# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO PRODUCE Spaceship.webm (run with a modern FFmpeg build)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source: D:\download\Spaceship2.mp4 (green-screen ship, 24 fps, 5.04s)
#
# ffmpeg -y -i D:/download/Spaceship2.mp4 \
#   -filter_complex "[0:v]scale=-2:480,chromakey=green:0.1:0.1,setpts=0.667*PTS[out]" \
#   -map "[out]" -c:v libvpx -pix_fmt yuva420p -auto-alt-ref 0 -b:v 1M \
#   Spaceship.webm
#
# What each part does:
#   scale=-2:480          -> 480p output (width auto)
#   chromakey=green:0.1:0.1 -> green (0,255,0) background -> transparent
#   setpts=0.667*PTS      -> speed up 50% (1.5x). Omit for normal speed.
#   -c:v libvpx           -> VP8, the only WebM codec FFmpeg supports with alpha
#   -pix_fmt yuva420p     -> includes the alpha (transparency) channel
#   -auto-alt-ref 0       -> REQUIRED so VP8 keeps its alpha track
#   -b:v 1M               -> target bitrate
#
# NOTE: leave out setpts for a normal loop, or add split/reverse/concat for a
# ping-pong loop. Verify with: ffmpeg -v verbose -i Spaceship.webm (look for
# "alpha_mode: 1"). Spaceship.webm is NOT ignored and should be committed.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------